OL,3,GNEWSABattery fire warning after 'sharp
OL,4,Arise' in incidents
OL,5,
OL,6,FResidents have been asked to dispose of
OL,7,Fbatteries responsibly following a
OL,8,F"sharp rise" in fires linked to waste
OL,9,Fcollections.
OL,11,FWest Northamptonshire Council said the
OL,12,Fnumber of such fires had increased from
OL,13,Fone in 2023-24 to 35 in 2025-26.
OL,15,FThe increase mirrors national concern
OL,16,Fabout lithium-ion batteries being
OL,17,Fplaced in household waste and recycling
OL,18,Fbins, where they can be crushed or
OL,19,Fdamaged during collection and
OL,20,Fprocessing, and then catch fire.
OL,23,APub: 30-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBC Eng (E) NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,368,360,200,160,0,100
